---
title: Lesson page
layout: home
description: The player layout — the lesson filling the page, the curriculum beside it, and one button that does the only thing anybody wants next. Nothing else on the screen.
eyebrow: Collections · Course
source: src/components/curriculum.css · video.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Course · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide" id="lesson-layout" data-sidebar="on" style="--im-single-aside: 21rem">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1.5rem">
		{{#with demo.lessons.[2]}}
		<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .75rem">
			<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="flex: 1">
				<ol class="im-breadcrumb im-breadcrumb-chevron">
					<li><a href="/collections/course/">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}}<span>Design tokens, properly</span></a></li>
					<li><a href="/collections/course/">{{> "icons/layers"}}<span>The token layer</span></a></li>
					<li><span aria-current="page">Lesson {{n}}</span></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>
			<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button" id="rail-show" hidden onclick="document.getElementById('lesson-layout').dataset.sidebar='on';this.hidden=true">{{icon "panel-right"}}Lessons</button>
			<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-lessonmenu-trigger" type="button" popovertarget="lessons-sheet" onclick="document.getElementById('lessons-sheet').showModal()">{{icon "list"}}Lessons <span class="im-hint" style="margin:0">3/7</span></button>
		</div>

		<div class="im-video im-video-full" id="lesson" data-im-video="aqz-KE-bpKQ" data-im-video-title="{{title}}">
			<img class="im-video-poster" src="{{lookup ../demo.shots shot}}" alt="" loading="eager">
			<button class="im-video-play" type="button" aria-label="Play">{{> "icons/play"}}</button>
		</div>

		<header class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .5rem">
			<p class="im-snipcard-meta"><span class="im-lesson-kind">{{icon "square-play"}}Video</span><span>{{time}}</span><span>Lesson {{n}} of 07</span></p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title" style="font-size: var(--im-text-h2)">{{title}}</h1>
			<p class="im-lede" style="margin: 0">{{text}}</p>
		</header>
		{{/with}}

		<section class="im-section" style="--im-section-gap: .75rem">
			<h2 class="im-caption">Chapters</h2>
			<ol class="im-chapters" data-im-chapters="#lesson" data-im-duration="14:05" aria-label="Chapters">
				<li><button type="button" data-t="0:00"><time>0:00</time><span>What we are fixing</span></button></li>
				<li><button type="button" data-t="2:40"><time>2:40</time><span>The two blocks, written out</span></button></li>
				<li><button type="button" data-t="7:15"><time>7:15</time><span>Why a reference cycle throws both away</span></button></li>
				<li><button type="button" data-t="11:30"><time>11:30</time><span>Testing it properly</span></button></li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush">
			<h2>The two blocks</h2>
			<p>Dark mode is not a filter and it is not a second stylesheet. It is the <strong>semantic</strong> layer, written twice — once under the light theme and once under the dark one — with the primitives untouched in both.</p>
			<pre><code class="language-css">:root {
	--im-canvas: var(--im-white);
	--im-ink: var(--im-gray-950);
}

:root[data-theme="dark"] {
	--im-canvas: var(--im-gray-950);
	--im-ink: var(--im-white);
}</code></pre>
			<p>Two <strong>literal</strong> blocks. Not <code>--a: var(--b); --b: var(--a)</code> — that is a reference cycle, and CSS throws both declarations away without a word in the console. It is the single most common way this goes wrong, and it took me an afternoon the first time.</p>

			<figure class="im-shot">
				<img src="{{demo.shots.[2]}}" alt="" loading="lazy">
				<figcaption><b>Both themes, one component.</b> The card names no colour at all — only <code>--im-surface</code> and <code>--im-ink</code>.</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<h2>What to check before you move on</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>A component with a hard-coded colour in it. There should be none; grep for <code>#</code>.</li>
				<li>An inverted block — a dark footer on a light page — which needs its own two literal blocks for the same reason.</li>
				<li><code>color-scheme</code> on anything inverted, or the scrollbars and form controls stay the wrong way round.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<nav class="im-lessonnav" aria-label="Lessons">
			<a class="im-lessonnav-item" href="/collections/course/lesson/" rel="prev">
				<img src="{{demo.shots.[1]}}" alt="" loading="lazy">
				<span>
					<small>{{icon "arrow-left"}}Previous · Lesson 02</small>
					<b>Primitives and semantics</b>
				</span>
			</a>
			<a class="im-lessonnav-item" href="/collections/course/lesson/" rel="next" data-next>
				<img src="{{demo.shots.[3]}}" alt="" loading="lazy">
				<span>
					<small>Next · Lesson 04{{icon "arrow-right"}}</small>
					<b>The page shell</b>
				</span>
			</a>
		</nav>

		{{> "components/comments" thread=demo.comments count="24" lean=true limit="1"}}
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail im-sticky-rail-full">
			<nav class="im-curriculum im-rail-grow" aria-label="Lessons">
				<div class="im-curriculum-head">
					<p class="im-curriculum-title">{{icon "graduation-cap"}}Design tokens, properly</p>
					<button class="im-curriculum-close" type="button" aria-label="Hide the lessons" onclick="document.getElementById('lesson-layout').dataset.sidebar='off';document.getElementById('rail-show').hidden=false">{{icon "panel-right"}}</button>
					<p class="im-curriculum-progress"><span>2 of 7</span><span class="im-progress" role="progressbar" aria-label="Through the course" aria-valuenow="29" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" style="--im-value: .29"></span></p>
				</div>
				{{#each demo.sections}}
				<p class="im-module-meta" style="padding: .75rem 1rem .25rem">{{n}} · {{name}}</p>
				<ol class="im-lessons im-lessons-shots">
					{{#each ../demo.lessons}}{{#match n ">=" ../from}}{{#match n "<=" ../to}}
					<li><a class="im-lesson" href="/collections/course/lesson/" data-state="{{#if locked}}locked{{else}}{{state}}{{/if}}"{{#match state "=" "current"}} aria-current="page"{{/match}}><span class="im-lesson-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="im-lesson-shot"><img src="{{lookup @root.demo.shots shot}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span>{{title}}</span><small>{{time}}</small></a></li>
					{{/match}}{{/match}}{{/each}}
				</ol>
				{{/each}}
			</nav>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<dialog class="im-lessonmenu" id="lessons-sheet" aria-label="Lessons">
	<nav class="im-curriculum">
		<div class="im-curriculum-head">
			<p class="im-curriculum-title">{{icon "graduation-cap"}}Design tokens, properly</p>
			<button class="im-curriculum-close" type="button" aria-label="Close" onclick="this.closest('dialog').close()">{{icon "x"}}</button>
			<p class="im-curriculum-progress"><span>2 of 7</span><span class="im-progress" role="progressbar" aria-label="Through the course" aria-valuenow="29" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" style="--im-value: .29"></span></p>
		</div>
		<ol class="im-lessons">
			{{#each demo.lessons}}
			<li>
				<a class="im-lesson" href="/collections/course/lesson/" data-state="{{#if locked}}locked{{else}}{{state}}{{/if}}"{{#match state "=" "current"}} aria-current="page"{{/match}}>
					<span class="im-lesson-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<span>{{title}}</span>
					<small>{{time}}</small>
				</a>
			</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ol>
	</nav>
</dialog>

<section class="im-section im-wrap"><div class="im-prose">
<p>The lessons sit on the <strong>right</strong>, in a rail that fills the window; the panel-right button collapses it (<code>data-sidebar="off"</code> on the single layout) and the same button in the header brings it back. Each row carries its still and its length. Under 64rem the rail becomes the <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> sheet opened from the header. Chapters, previous/next with the still, and lean comments below the player.</p>
</div></section>
